// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/rental_terms.t27 -- the rental term ladder, the published term-discount
; bands, and the one rounding rule every total is built from.
; Canonical source of truth for the INTEGER basis-point form of the term arithmetic that D15
; puts in src/trios/pricing.rs, so the Axum server and the Dioxus/WASM client are checked against
; one written contract instead of against each other. An earlier working-tree draft at
; specs/rental_terms.t27 stated the same bands in f64; its declarations were semantically
; classified in docs/t27-semantic-merge-matrix.md and this canonical file is the chosen owner.
; That draft is GONE and no reviewer can reopen it: it was never tracked, so it is not in the
; history either (git log --all -- specs/rental_terms.t27 prints nothing, re-verified 2026-09-21
; and still empty). The COUNT that used to stand beside that fact has not held: this sentence
; said specs/ holds twelve tracked files, and on 2026-09-21 it holds FORTY-THREE --
; specs/agents/turbobaby.t27 plus the 42 under specs/turbobaby/. The corpus more than tripled
; and the sentence went on stating twelve, which is why the live count is pinned below as
; CORPUS_FILES rather than left in prose. (Stale again within the day: re-measured 2026-09-22 it
; holds FORTY-FIVE, 44 of them under specs/turbobaby/, and the pinned constant did not notice --
; the note above CORPUS_FILES says why.) What the number was there to support is unchanged and
; is the part worth checking: there is still no root-level .t27 in specs/ at all. The TWIN_* constants
; below name the path it occupied and the matrix that absorbed it -- not a second authority,
; and not a file that still exists.
; Transcribed from data/fleet_seed.json (measured_at 2026-09-12):
; term_discount_bands, reconciliation.checks, and the NMAX 155 row of families. Nothing
; below is a client price; see WHAT THIS NEVER DOES. ASCII only (L3), English only.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-12). Of the 710 client dialogs / 31245 messages behind KB_faq,
; 481 messages are about dates and term -- the fifth topic by volume, above deposit (375)
; and availability (180) -- and the term rule lived in no file in this repository.
; Writing it down measured three things issue #17 could not know.
; --
; 1. THE BANDS ARE INTERVALS, NOT MULTIPLIERS: week [0.06, 0.15], two_weeks
;    [0.15, 0.25], month [0.35, 0.50]. The issue asks for an invariant that a longer term
;    carries a LOWER daily rate, and reads as though the discount for a longer term were
;    strictly greater. That is FALSE at one edge: week's ceiling of 0.15 IS two_weeks'
;    floor of 0.15, so the consecutive bands touch and are not disjoint. A week at its
;    best published discount and a fortnight at its worst carry the SAME daily rate --
;    382 THB on the 449 NMAX 155 tariff, pinned in a test below. The claim this file
;    states is therefore NON-INCREASING (>=, not >), stated on a well-defined
;    representative of each band: floor against floor and ceiling against ceiling.
;    The touching is not a defect in the tariff. A band is a negotiating range that a
;    human closes inside, not a formula; adjacent ranges that share an endpoint leave no
;    term unpriced, whereas disjoint ranges would. The other junction is the one with a
;    hole in it: two_weeks' ceiling 0.25 to month's floor 0.35 is a gap of 0.10 that the
;    tariff publishes nothing for, and that gap is pinned below too.
; --
; 2. SIX RUNGS AGAINST THREE BANDS, AND FOUR RUNGS WITH NO BAND AT ALL.
;    observed_terms_days is [7, 30, 90, 120, 150, 180], which DOES match the issue's
;    "7 days, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6 months" at 30 days to the month (90/30 = 3, 180/30 = 6). The
;    days are used here because they are unambiguous. But no band is published beyond the
;    month, so four of the six rungs -- 90, 120, 150 and 180 -- have NO published discount
;    at all. This file READS the month band as "a month or longer" (band_index_for_days),
;    and under that reading those four rungs inherit the 30-day rung's rate and the ladder
;    comes out FLAT from 30 days on. The flat tail is therefore a property of the READING,
;    not of the tariff, so it is not independent evidence about monotonicity: only the
;    touching edge in (1) is, and that one is published. The reading is recorded here, and
;    made explicit in the function, precisely so that nobody mistakes it for a measurement.
; --
; 3. THE BANDS REPRODUCE NO PUBLISHED PRICE -- AND THE TWO POSSIBLE BASES DISAGREE ABOUT
;    HOW BADLY. 12 of the 14 in-stock families publish both a daily tariff and a monthly
;    low-season figure. Measured AGAINST THE PRE-CLASS-DISCOUNT BASE TARIFF, the per-day
;    discount each pair implies runs from 0.618 (FORZA 300: 7900/30 = 263.33 against a 690
;    tariff) to 0.665 (NINJA 400: 11900/30 = 396.67 against 1185) -- all 12 above the month
;    band's 0.50 ceiling, not one inside the band. But the seed nowhere states whether
;    monthly_low_season_thb is PRE or POST class discount, and the base tariff is the very
;    number field_notes.base_rate_thb_day and D11 forbid using as a client rate. On the
;    post-class-discount basis the same 12 pairs imply 0.491 to 0.606, and TWO of them fall
;    INSIDE the published month band: FORZA 300 at 0.4911 (263.33 against 690 x 0.75 =
;    517.50) and XMAX 300 at 0.4993 (296.67 against 592.50). FORZA 300 is the same family
;    that supplies the 0.618 extremum above. So this arithmetic does not settle the question
;    either way, and it reverses between two bases of which the seed publishes neither --
;    which is itself the reason a band is not a price. Both bases are pinned in a test below.
;    On NMAX 155, applying the month band at its most generous published bound to the
;    PRE-class-discount 449 gives 225 x 30 = 6750 against a published 5000, 1750 THB apart;
;    applying the same bound to the class-discounted 337/day -- the seed's own reconciled
;    grid figure -- gives 169 x 30 = 5070, 70 THB apart. A quantity whose size moves by a
;    factor of 25 with an unpublished assumption is not a price. Season and term are
;    different axes, and that is exactly the point -- this arithmetic is an audit
;    instrument, not a price path.
; --
; WHAT THIS NEVER DOES: it never produces a client quote. D11 -- the client-facing price
; is the number the door (the owner's live sheet) returns; when the door is silent the
; bot says a human quotes this price and emits NO number at all: not exact, not a "from"
; number, not an average, not a range, and not silence either. Every function here is
; named audit_ for that reason, BANDS_PRODUCE_CLIENT_QUOTES is pinned false by an
; invariant, and no function takes a term alone and returns a price: a discount in basis
; points must be supplied by the caller, because the tariff publishes a range and a range
; is not a number. It pins the TERM axis, the rounding, and -- since 2026-09-20 -- the two
; published CLASS RATES, which until that date were declared in no canonical contract at all.
; What it did not pin until 2026-09-21 is how those two tables COMPOSE. The sentence that
; stood here said that was "unspecified by the seed and is therefore left open here, pinned
; open by a constant rather than closed by a guess", and it was true of the seed when it was
; written: data/fleet_seed.json publishes two tables and no order between them, and still does.
; It was never true of the SHOP. The owner's knowledge base -- the brain -- states the price
; model as a formula, and that formula is a PRODUCT OF THREE FACTORS: model base x season
; factor x term step. In it the seed's class_discounts is not a third axis at all, but the
; magnitude of the season factor at one named place in the calendar. Read live on 2026-09-21
; from brain:business_rules and declared below in THE COMPOSITION, where what is still refused
; is refused BY NAME: the month-by-month coefficient table, which lives in a sheet this side
; does not own. See THE CLASS TABLE and THE COMPOSITION.
; It also holds no customer, no contract and no payment history (D14): the totals below are
; pinned against the published tariff of one catalogue model and against the six
; reconciliation rows, and against nothing else.
; --
; A cheap check this file deliberately does not rely on: that the totals "look right".
; Any total is self-consistent with the function that produced it, so agreeing with
; itself proves nothing -- the same way a licence file named .t27 compiles. The rounding
; test therefore reproduces the six grid figures MEASURED by someone else (704, 749, 518,
; 593, 337, 2091) from the six published base tariffs, and half-down would miss three.
; An earlier revision of this paragraph claimed those six figures are pinned a second time in
; specs/pricing_honesty.t27, through round_half_up_baht and a RECONCILED_DOOR_THB row loop.
; Measured 2026-09-20 both halves were false, and re-measured 2026-09-21 over the 43-file corpus
; the first still is: grep -rn RECONCILED_DOOR_THB specs/ matches only this file's own two lines
; and no other file. The second half needs one correction. It said pricing_honesty.t27 contains
; NONE of the six figures; it contains ONE of them. 337 appears there twice -- once against an
; orders.rs reconciliation gap of 0.4 baht, and once in a sentence that credits this contract's
; audit_daily_thb with pinning 449 at 2500 bp to 337. Neither is a second reproduction of the
; measured column: the first is a different quantity and the second points back here by name.
; So the conclusion holds and its supporting absence does not, which is stated in that order on
; purpose -- a reader who finds the 337 must not conclude the paragraph was bluffing about the
; rest. The other five figures (704, 749, 518, 593, 2091) appear in that file nowhere. The
; second pinning lived in the deleted f64 draft and went with it. So this file is the ONLY
; place the externally measured column is reproduced, and the cross-check the old paragraph
; advertised does not exist. That is stated rather than quietly dropped, because a reader who
; believed it would go looking for a second arithmetic that is not there. One arithmetic
; against one outside measurement is what this file actually offers.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module rental-terms;

pub const KIND : str = "terms";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/rental-terms";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby rental term ladder and term-discount bands";
; Current t27c does not support brace imports. This metadata records that pricing honesty owns
; the live door authority; rental terms neither imports nor redeclares that fact.
pub const REUSES_PRICING_ID : str = "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
; The same device for the class axis. bike-catalog.t27 owns the class algebra -- CLASSES,
; CLASS_SCOOTER, CLASS_MOTORCYCLE, CLASS_COUNT, CLASS_NONE -- and says so in its own header.
; The class-discount table below is therefore keyed on the seed's own class STRINGS, which are
; the literal keys of class_discounts and the literal values of families[].class, and it
; declares no second copy of that algebra: no discriminant, no count, no class-name array.
; Named by ID and never by line, because a line citation ages and this one would age fast.
pub const REUSES_CATALOG_ID : str = "turbobaby/bike-catalog";
pub const SOURCE : str = "data/fleet_seed.json";
pub const SOURCE_MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-12";
pub const TARIFF_SOURCE_ID : str = "KB_faq";
; D15: one implementation of the price arithmetic. This spec is the written contract for the
; part of it named below in THE COMPOSITION -- the term axis and the rounding -- and not for
; all three of D15's jobs.
pub const IMPLEMENTATION : str = "src/trios/pricing.rs";

; --- THE ROOT TWIN: retained until the declaration matrix is independently reviewed --------
; specs/rental_terms.t27 carries the legacy ID below and states the same tariff in f64. The
; merge matrix maps its interval lookup to band_index_for_days, its f64 bounds to the exact BP
; bounds here, its monthly non-derivation to the two monthly audit tests, and its class-discount
; helpers to the separate pricing axis. That resolves ownership without pretending the two
; rounding paths are identical: this file rounds the daily rate before multiplying; the legacy
; diagnostic rounded the total. The draft itself is gone and was never tracked, so the matrix
; is now the only record of it; TWIN_SPEC_PATH is the path it occupied, kept so the mapping
; stays greppable, and TWIN_IS_RESOLVED means every one of its declarations has an outcome --
; not that a file was removed.
pub const TWIN_SPEC_PATH : str = "specs/rental_terms.t27";
pub const TWIN_SPEC_ID : str = "turbobaby/rental_terms";
pub const TWIN_ENCODING : str = "legacy f64 fractions mapped to canonical integer basis points";
pub const TWIN_MERGE_MATRIX : str = "docs/t27-semantic-merge-matrix.md";
pub const TWIN_IS_RESOLVED : bool = true;
; The corpus this file measures itself against, as a number rather than as a word. Two
; paragraphs above counted it in prose -- "twelve tracked files", "the eleven files under
; specs/turbobaby/" -- and both were true when written and wrong by 2026-09-21. A word cannot
; fail; this can. CORPUS_ROOT_T27_FILES is the claim those counts were actually supporting: the
; deleted draft's slot at the root of specs/ is still empty, and that is what makes
; TWIN_SPEC_PATH a former address rather than a competing authority.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22: "this can" fail was not true, and the counts are re-measured. The first five
; constants below are KEPT as the 2026-09-21 reading -- 43, 42, 1 and 0, and its date. At a33e500,
; git ls-files specs and the glob specs/**/*.t27 both give 45, specs/turbobaby/*.t27 gives 44,
; specs/agents/*.t27 still gives 1 and specs/*.t27 still matches nothing; that reading sits beside
; the first as the *_REMEASURED constants, dated by CORPUS_REMEASURED_AT. 14b01ac (2026-09-21 21:49
; +0700) added specs/turbobaby/order_presentation.t27 and specs/turbobaby/person_naming.t27 after
; the first count was taken, and the invariant on these numbers stayed green because it compares
; this file's own constants with each other: nothing reads the tree. Both are a DATED READING --
; re-measure and re-date them, do not read them as a live check. They are also deliberately not
; bound in scripts/verify_t27_against_source.py: a count of the corpus bound as a live check would
; go red on every new spec, which is the corpus growing and not this contract drifting. The claim
; they support, an empty root, holds in both readings.
pub const CORPUS_FILES : u8 = 43;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_UNDER_TURBOBABY : u8 = 42;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_UNDER_AGENTS : u8 = 1;
pub const CORPUS_ROOT_T27_FILES : u8 = 0;
pub const CORPUS_MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
pub const CORPUS_FILES_REMEASURED : u8 = 45;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_UNDER_TURBOBABY_REMEASURED : u8 = 44;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_UNDER_AGENTS_REMEASURED : u8 = 1;
pub const CORPUS_ROOT_T27_FILES_REMEASURED : u8 = 0;
pub const CORPUS_REMEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";

; --- D11, the rule that outranks everything in this file ----------------------------------
; These bands never become a client quote. The door answers, or a human does.
pub const BANDS_PRODUCE_CLIENT_QUOTES : bool = false;
; RESOLVED 2026-09-24: WHAT A SILENT DOOR IS ANSWERED WITH is not this file's to word. Until this
; edit the next line declared it here as ON_SILENCE -- a string equal to the agent charter's
; PRICE_ON_SILENCE and already worded apart from the owner's -- although the edge above says this
; file neither imports nor redeclares the door's rule. turbobaby/pricing-honesty (REUSES_PRICING_ID)
; owns what an absent price renders as: the dash carrying SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES, whose sentence is its
; MUST_SAY. Nothing in this file read ON_SILENCE, so it is dropped and listed in
; RESTATEMENT_DROPPED_ON_RESOLUTION rather than kept as a copy; the shape followed is
; turbobaby/delivery-terms' OFF_LADDER_NOTE, which names that renderer and declares no sentence.
pub const SILENCE_SENTENCE_IS_DECLARED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const PRICING_SILENCE_DECLARATIONS : [2]str = ["SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES", "MUST_SAY"];

; --- the term ladder, in days -------------------------------------------------------------
; Exactly term_discount_bands.observed_terms_days. Days, not months: the issue names
; "7 days, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6 months" and the two ladders agree at 30 days to the month, but
; only the days are unambiguous, so the days are what is pinned.
pub const TERM_DAYS : [6]i32 = [7, 30, 90, 120, 150, 180];
pub const DAYS_PER_WEEK : i32 = 7;
; 2 x 7. The fortnight is the two_weeks band's own name in days; it is NOT a rung of the
; measured ladder -- no observed term falls between 7 and 30 days.
pub const DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT : i32 = 14;
; The conversion that makes the issue's month ladder equal the measured days: 30, 90, 120,
; 150 and 180 divided by 30 give 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6.
pub const DAYS_PER_MONTH : i32 = 30;

; --- the three published bands, as intervals ----------------------------------------------
; Basis points, because a band bound is a fraction and this language pins integer widths.
; Read straight off term_discount_bands: 0.06 x 10000 = 600, 0.15 -> 1500, 0.25 -> 2500,
; 0.35 -> 3500, 0.50 -> 5000. An integer bound cannot drift by a rounding mode, and
; nothing here needs a float.
pub const BP_ONE : i32 = 10000;
pub const BAND_NAMES : [3]str = ["week", "two_weeks", "month"];
pub const WEEK_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP : i32 = 600;
pub const WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP : i32 = 1500;
pub const TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP : i32 = 1500;
pub const TWO_WEEKS_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP : i32 = 2500;
pub const MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP : i32 = 3500;
pub const MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP : i32 = 5000;
; Below a week the tariff publishes no term band at all. That is an absence, not a zero:
; a short rental is charged at the tariff the door quotes, and this file does not invent a
; band for it (D9: absent stays absent).
pub const BAND_NONE : i8 = -1;

; --- THE CLASS TABLE: the other published discount axis -----------------------------------
; data/fleet_seed.json "class_discounts", lines 105-109 as measured 2026-09-20: scooter 0.25
; on line 107, motorcycle 0.15 on line 108, under a $comment stating that the base rates in
; families are PRE-discount. On the basis-point axis this file already owns: 0.25 -> 2500 and
; 0.15 -> 1500. EXACT, not rounded -- both fractions are exact multiples of 1/10000, and the
; test below proves that in integers instead of asserting it in a comment.
; Stored the same way downstream: migrations/079_rental_terms.sql inserts the same two pairs
; and CHECKs class IN ('scooter', 'motorcycle'), so the two published classes are a closed set
; in the database as well as in the seed.
; --
; WHY THIS FILE, measured 2026-09-20. Until this edit the value was declared in NO canonical
; contract: grep -rnE "SCOOTER_DISCOUNT|MOTORCYCLE_DISCOUNT" over specs/ returned nothing but
; the stale paragraph in this file's own test section, which named two root-level specs as the
; declaration sites. Those files are gone, so a published rate was travelling in prose only --
; pricing_honesty.t27 and ride_game.t27 each mention "scooter 0.25, motorcycle 0.15" in a
; comment, and a comment is not a declaration. The rate is pinned here because this file
; already owns the integer form of the discount arithmetic; the class algebra it is keyed on
; stays bike-catalog.t27's (REUSES_CATALOG_ID). The correction is in the tests section below.
; RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21 over the 43-file corpus, and the absence still holds: that grep matches
; three lines, all of them in this file. One thing has changed in this file's favour and is
; recorded because a re-measurement that only ever confirms is not a re-measurement --
; turbobaby/ride-game now carries a declared CLASS_DISCOUNT_QUOTE_NOTE which states that it
; declares no class discount and names turbobaby/rental-terms as the owner of
; SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP and MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP. The prose-only travel described
; above has therefore ended on both sides: the rate is declared here, and the neighbour that
; used to mention it in a comment now points at this file by ID instead.
pub const SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP : i32 = 2500;
pub const MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP : i32 = 1500;
; Fails closed. 0 means "this input publishes no class discount", NOT "a discount of zero":
; handed to audit_daily_thb it returns the tariff unchanged, which is the 33% scooter
; overstatement D9 and D11 forbid, and a test below pins exactly that trap so the sentinel
; cannot be mistaken for a rate. The runtime says the same in its own words -- src/db/bikes.rs
; discount_for_class returns an Option, and its doc calls None "the caller's cue that no price
; may be computed - not a cue to fall back to no discount". A caller BRANCHES on this value.
pub const CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE : i32 = 0;
; A measured asymmetry between the two rates, 2026-09-20. All six rows of
; reconciliation.checks -- XMAX 300 NEW, ADV 350, FORZA 300, XMAX 300, NMAX 155, XADV 750 --
; read class "scooter" in families[], so the 2500 is corroborated against the owner's own
; quote sheet six times over and the 1500 is corroborated by no row of that grid at all.
; That does not leave the 1500 unevidenced: field_notes.base_rate_thb_day says displaying the
; tariff raw "overstates every scooter by 33% and every motorcycle by 18%", an independent
; sentence in the same seed, and both figures are recomputed from these two constants in a
; test below. Declared false rather than left unsaid, so that nobody reads the six-row
; reconciliation as covering both rates.
pub const MOTORCYCLE_RATE_IS_GRID_RECONCILED : bool = false;

; --- the one tariff this file computes with -----------------------------------------------
; NMAX 155: 449 THB/day published base (PRE class discount -- rendering it as a client
; price without the class discount overstates every scooter by 33%), the largest family in
; the fleet at 10 of 37 units, and one of the six reconciliation rows. A reference for
; arithmetic, never a quote. Its published monthly low-season figure is carried too, because
; it is the measurement the month band fails to reproduce on EITHER basis -- 6750 against it
; pre class discount, 5070 post -- and a bound that misses the published figure both ways is
; not a price on either.
; WHOSE 449 THIS IS (resolved 2026-09-24). The choice of NMAX 155 as the reference, and all the
; arithmetic done with it, are this file's. The published day rate itself is not: it is nmax-155's
; base_rate_thb_day in data/fleet_seed.json, and turbobaby/pricing-honesty (REUSES_PRICING_ID)
; declares it as CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB -- that file owns the published-rate census, of
; which "the cheapest rate on a family with units" is one reading. Until this edit both files
; declared 449 in the present tense with no edge between the two declarations, and a review of
; 2026-09-23 found neither bound by a gate. The copy stays here, because forty-odd assertions below
; compute with it and the pinned compiler carries no constant across files
; (SHARED_VOCABULARY_IMPORT_IS_NOT_SHIPPED in turbobaby/ride-game); what changed is that it is
; declared a copy of a named owner, and gate 3 binds it and the owner's to the same seed row, so a
; one-sided edit turns red instead of shipping.
pub const REF_MODEL : str = "NMAX 155";
pub const REF_BASE_THB_DAY : i32 = 449;
pub const REF_BASE_IS_A_COPY : bool = true;
pub const REF_BASE_OWNER_DECLARATION : str = "CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB";
pub const REF_BASE_SEED_FAMILY : str = "nmax-155";
pub const REF_MONTHLY_LOW_SEASON_THB : i32 = 5000;
pub const RESTATEMENT_DROPPED_ON_RESOLUTION : [1]str = ["ON_SILENCE"];
pub const RESTATEMENTS_RESOLVED_AT : str = "2026-09-24";

; --- the arithmetic -----------------------------------------------------------------------

; Half-up to the baht, integers only: scale by the net basis points, then divide by BP_ONE
; with half a unit added first, which is what half-up IS for a non-negative number --
; (2n + d) / 2d under a truncating divide. Every operand here is non-negative, so the
; truncation is a floor, which is what the added half requires. The scale and the round are
; one step on purpose: that is what makes this the integer form rather than a second copy of
; specs/pricing_honesty.t27's round_half_up_baht, which rounds an f64 that someone else has
; already scaled.
; Half-up is measured, not chosen: every one of the six reconciliation rows is the base
; tariff x 0.75 rounded half-up (748.5 -> 749, 592.5 -> 593, 517.5 -> 518), and half-down
; would miss three of the six.
; The DISCOUNT may be negative, and since 2026-09-21 that is a declared property rather than
; an accident of the arithmetic. Under the shop's published sign convention a minus IS a
; surcharge (see THE COMPOSITION), so base x (BP_ONE - discount_bp) moves the price UP for a
; negative discount_bp -- through this same line, with no second code path and no second
; rounding rule. What has to stay non-negative is `scaled`, and it does for every discount_bp
; at or below BP_ONE; a discount_bp ABOVE BP_ONE would make it negative and break the half-up,
; and no published band or class rate comes near that.
; An absent or negative tariff never reaches this function. D9's honesty filter drops it
; upstream and a family with no published rate is not priced at all -- CLICK 125 is the
; single instance (totals.families_without_published_rate = 1) and it is closed to new
; rentals anyway (D12).
pub fn audit_daily_thb(base_thb_day: i32, discount_bp: i32) i32 {
    const scaled = base_thb_day * (BP_ONE - discount_bp);
    return (scaled * 2 + BP_ONE) / (BP_ONE * 2);
}

; The total cost of a term. The ORDER is pinned here rather than left to the caller: round
; the daily rate to the baht FIRST, then multiply by the days. The owner's own sheet works
; that way -- its stale CLICK row reads 187/day and 935 for 5 nights, and 187 x 5 = 935
; exactly, a rounded per-day figure times nights. (Cited for the shape of the arithmetic
; only; that row is stale as a tariff, see pricing_policy.not_offered.)
; The order is worth a decision: rounding the total instead gives 291.85 x 30 = 8755.5 ->
; 8756 where this gives 292 x 30 = 8760, a 4 THB divergence on one month of one model.
; Note what is NOT claimed: the total is not monotone in the term. A longer term costs
; more in total. It is the per-DAY rate that never rises.
pub fn audit_total_thb(base_thb_day: i32, discount_bp: i32, days: i32) i32 {
    return audit_daily_thb(base_thb_day, discount_bp) * days;
}

; --- THE COMPOSITION, as the shop publishes it --------------------------------------------
; D15 gives src/trios/pricing.rs three jobs: the class discount, the term discount, and
; half-up rounding to the baht. This file is the written contract for the term axis and the
; rounding, and -- since 2026-09-21 -- for the SHAPE those two published tables compose in.
; --
; WHAT STOOD HERE, AND WHY THE REFUSAL WAS RIGHT. Until 2026-09-21 this section said: "How the
; two discounts COMPOSE is deliberately NOT pinned, because the seed does not publish it:
; class_discounts and term_discount_bands are two tables with no stated order between them,
; and audit_daily_thb takes exactly one discount for that reason", and it closed with
; "Nothing shows which way this one works, so it is pinned OPEN". Every clause of that is
; STILL TRUE ABOUT THE SEED, and the refusal was the right answer to the question as asked.
; What was wrong was the reach of the word "nothing": the seed is not the only thing that
; publishes here, and the shop's own written rules had never been read. They were read on
; 2026-09-21, and they answer -- with an answer bigger than an ordering.
; --
; THE SOURCE, AND HOW IT IS CITED. The owner's knowledge base is not a file in this
; repository, so it is cited as brain:<node>:<line> and never as a path: no path would
; resolve, and a reader who cannot tell a repository file from a foreign one cannot tell what
; this side may fix from what it may only read. Everything below was read on 2026-09-21 from a
; read-only dump of node business_rules. That node keeps two kinds of fact apart on purpose,
; and so does this section, because they carry different weight and are argued with different
; instruments: a rule the OWNER STATED on a named date -- which the node marks as NOT verified
; by data and as OVERRIDING anything derived from booking history -- and a quantity MEASURED
; off the bookings base, which carries a corpus size and a date. Flattening those into "the
; rule says" would throw away the one distinction that makes half of this arguable with
; numbers and the other half not.
; One more property of the source, stated once and not repeated at every quotation mark: the
; node is written in Russian, and this corpus is ASCII and English (L3). Every quoted sentence
; below is therefore a TRANSLATION and not a transcription -- the numbers, the dates and the
; citations cross unchanged, the wording does not. A reader checking a quotation should expect
; to find the fact at the cited line, not the string.
; --
; 1. THE COMPOSITION IS A PRODUCT OF THREE FACTORS, not an order between two discounts.
;    brain:business_rules:228-229 states the price model as a formula: the daily price is the
;    MODEL BASE times the SEASON factor of the period times the TERM STEP of the bucket. The
;    same sentence stands at brain:business_rules:157-160 as a consequence of the seasonal
;    calendar, so it is not a stray line. Two things follow at once. Multiplication commutes,
;    so "which discount is applied first" was never the question the seed left open -- factors
;    of a product have no order to publish. What the seed's silence does leave open is where
;    the ROUNDING falls between the factors, and that is still unpublished: the old tripwire
;    stays alive there, as COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_IS_PINNED, which is the one place it still
;    belongs. The arithmetic that made the old refusal worth having is unchanged and still
;    pinned in a test below: 337 then 169 stepwise against 168 as one fused factor.
; 2. THE TWO CLASS RATES ARE A SEASONAL MAGNITUDE THAT DEPENDS ON CLASS, not a class axis.
;    This is what made the old framing WRONG rather than merely incomplete. In the owner's own
;    words on 2026-08-16, brain:business_rules:208-211 settles a dispute inside the node
;    itself: 25 percent for scooters and 15 percent for motorcycles are the FLOOR of the deep
;    low season, June to October, while 10 percent is the CEILING of the March-to-May
;    transition -- different places in the calendar, not a contradiction. Both halves of that
;    sentence name the DEEPEST discount at their own place, said the two ways the node says
;    them: the floor is the bottom of the price curve in the deep low season, and the ceiling
;    is the largest discount the transition is allowed to reach. They are not a minimum and a
;    maximum of one quantity, which is exactly the misreading the node was settling.
;    brain:business_rules:91-94 gives the same pair as the typical LOW SEASON magnitudes and
;    says "about" for each, which is the second reason they are not an axis: an axis does not
;    have a typical value. So SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP and MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP are
;    the integer form of the SEASON factor at one point of the calendar, and the term bands
;    are the other factor. The brain's "about" does not soften the seed: the seed publishes an
;    exact 0.25 and 0.15 and this file pins them exactly, while the brain says what those two
;    numbers MEAN and where in the year they sit. TRANSITION_CEILING_DISCOUNT_BP carries the
;    other named place, and note the coincidence it walks into -- 1000 bp is also the width of
;    the gap between the fortnight and month bands. Two axes, one integer, again.
; 3. THE SIGN IS INVERTED, AND THIS FILE ALREADY COMPUTES WITH IT.
;    brain:business_rules:86-90, the owner on 2026-08-15: a percentage WITHOUT a sign is a
;    DISCOUNT and moves the price DOWN; a percentage WITH A MINUS is a SURCHARGE and moves it
;    UP; and reading the minus as a discount puts the peak price about twenty percent below
;    where it belongs. The node marks this one NOT YET CONFIRMED BY DATA -- a measurement was
;    running when it was written -- and says to read it until then as the owner's intention
;    and not as a measured fact, so SIGN_CONVENTION_IS_DATA_CONFIRMED is declared false beside
;    it instead of being left unsaid. The trap is not in the arithmetic: audit_daily_thb
;    already moves the price the right way for a negative discount_bp. It is in a caller who
;    "fixes" the minus. On the reference tariff the two readings are 494 and 404 THB a day,
;    1821 basis points apart measured against the higher of the two.
;    CORRECTED 2026-09-21 BY REVIEW, and the withdrawn claim is kept in view. This paragraph
;    used to continue: the brain's "about twenty percent" is that ratio rounded -- 0.9/1.1,
;    which is base-independent, so the figure is a property of the convention rather than of
;    this tariff. Two things in that are wrong. FIRST, 1821 is not base-independent. The
;    convention alone gives 1 - 0.9/1.1 = 1818 bp; 1821 is what half-up rounding to the baht
;    does to that ratio at a base of 449, and a base of 1000 hands 1818 straight back. So the
;    constant is a figure about NMAX 155, and it is declared beside
;    SIGN_MISREAD_UNDERSTATEMENT_IS_BASE_INDEPENDENT = false and the unrounded 1818, with the
;    test below probing a second base so the retracted claim cannot quietly return. SECOND,
;    neither number is the brain's. The node says "about twenty percent" and names NO
;    denominator: measured against the BASE the gap is 0.2 of it, exactly twenty percent, and
;    measured against the correct price it is 18.18. Which one the owner meant is not
;    published, so no exact figure is attributed to him here and the hedge stays a hedge.
;    Pinned in a test and an invariant below, because a sign error of that size typechecks
;    perfectly.
;    WHAT IS NOT DECLARED HERE: the -10 percent above is the brain's OWN EXAMPLE in the sign
;    section, carried to show which way the arithmetic moves. It is not a peak rate this file
;    adopts. The three sections that state the peak magnitude as a rule carry the node's own
;    supersession marker (brain:business_rules:106, 156 and 194 hand them to the clarifications
;    of 2026-08-16), and no peak number is declared in this file at all.
; 4. WHOSE RULE THE CALENDAR IS, and the same supersession read honestly.
;    brain:business_rules:132-134, the owner on 2026-08-15, says the seasonal calendar is the
;    OWNER'S RULE and not a measurement: it OVERRIDES the price derived from booking history
;    and is NOT verified by data by construction, because the rule replaces the data rather
;    than following from it. That section is one of the three the node marks superseded, so
;    what this file carries is the restatement in the section that governs --
;    brain:business_rules:197-198, the owner on 2026-08-16, in the same words. Season is no
;    longer derived from bookings at all; the model base is the only factor still read off
;    them, on a window from 2024-01-01 (brain:business_rules:212-215), and the term step is
;    measured and window-independent (brain:business_rules:214). Presenting the calendar as a
;    measurement would be the same defect in the other direction as presenting a measurement
;    as a rule, so the three factors carry their provenance one by one in
;    COMPOSITION_FACTOR_PROVENANCE instead of sharing one word.
; 5. WHAT WAS VERIFIED WITH MONEY, AND THE FLOOR THAT CAME WITH IT.
;    brain:business_rules:234-241, measured 2026-08-15 and 2026-08-16 against completed
;    bookings: on the peak shelf of 20 December to 15 February the formula's median miss was
;    -0.6 percent over 260 bookings. The controls are what make that worth anything -- with no
;    season factor at all the miss is 21.4 percent, and with the owner's calendar 10.6 percent
;    -- and the node states the calendar earns 10.9 percentage points. This file carries all
;    three published figures AND the fact that they do not subtract: 21.4 minus 10.6 is 10.8,
;    one tenth of a point from the published 10.9, which is what three independently rounded
;    figures look like. None of the three is recomputed from the other two, because all three
;    are published, and inventing a fourth to reconcile them is the offence this file exists
;    against. (A different 10.9 stands at brain:business_rules:244-245 -- the SPREAD the
;    formula gets when the calendar is swapped for THE OWNER'S PERIODS, 10.9 percent where
;    this calendar's is 10.6 -- and it is not this quantity. CORRECTED 2026-09-21 BY REVIEW:
;    this parenthesis used to call that 10.9 "the SPREAD under a finer grid", which reverses
;    what the node says. Its heading is that subdividing the grid is EXHAUSTED -- a cell one
;    day wide gives the same 4.8 point bias as a monthly one, and the node reports no spread
;    for it at all -- and the 10.9 belongs to the move to the owner's periods, which the node
;    says made the numbers WORSE, 4.8 to 4.9 and 10.6 to 10.9. The claim that the two 10.9s
;    are different quantities is unchanged and is the only thing this parenthesis is for:
;    the same numeral, in one node, for two things.) The 10.6 percent is a FLOOR and not a
;    current error bar: the node says the
;    spread cannot be reduced, because haggling, the early-payment discount and the
;    agent-referred client all sit inside it and NONE of the three is observable in the
;    bookings base -- that base carries no booking date and no prepayment mark at all
;    (brain:business_rules:118-126), and the agent sign shows only in the dialogue
;    (brain:business_rules:115-116). Improvement waits on those three starting to be recorded
;    and on nothing else, which is why ACCURACY_FLOOR_IS_REDUCIBLE is false rather than absent.
;    For scale against this file's own arithmetic: 10.6 percent of the reference tariff is 47
;    THB a day, while the two divergences this file spends paragraphs on are 1 and 4 THB a day.
;    The small ones are still worth pinning -- they are two implementations of one rule
;    disagreeing, which is a defect -- but a reader who takes 1 THB for the width of the
;    uncertainty has the proportion backwards by a factor of forty-seven.
; 6. WHAT IS STILL REFUSED, and it is not the old refusal under a new name. The
;    month-by-month coefficient table -- the actual season numbers the formula multiplies by
;    -- is NOT declared here and must not be. brain:business_rules:95-96 says where it lives:
;    a price sheet inside the manager's spreadsheet, coefficients per month, set by the
;    manager, and that sheet is foreign and live, with read-only access from this side.
;    Declaring a number out of a live sheet nobody here owns is exactly the invention this
;    file exists to prevent, and it would go stale in silence, which is worse than being
;    absent. So the SHAPE of the composition is pinned and the CONTENT of its season factor is
;    not, and those are different claims: an implementation can now be checked for multiplying
;    three factors, and a season number still cannot be got out of this repository.
; --
; WHAT THIS STILL NEVER DOES. Declaring the shop's published price model does not make it a
; quote path, and nothing below may be served to a client as a price. D11 is untouched: the
; client-facing number is the one the door returns, and when the door is silent the answer
; says a human quotes this price and carries NO number -- not exact, not "from", not an
; average, not a range -- with silence forbidden as firmly as invention. The brain holds the
; primary record of that ruling in the owner's own words on 2026-09-12,
; brain:business_rules:1661-1678, which is the same ruling DECISIONS.md D11 states;
; turbobaby/pricing-honesty owns the rule and this file only says where it lives.
; RE-READ 2026-09-24, read-only, against the live node: 1661-1678 still holds the ruling's heading,
; the owner's two quoted sentences and the first two consequences (the live sheet is the client's
; price source; the 2026-08-17 construction is amended). The clause this paragraph paraphrases --
; the door silent, no number of any kind, silence forbidden like invention -- is the fourth
; consequence, at brain:business_rules:1684-1687, in the part the node labels as what follows from
; the owner's words without further inference. Both ranges are cited now so neither is read as
; the other.
; COMPOSITION_PRODUCES_CLIENT_QUOTES is tied to BANDS_PRODUCE_CLIENT_QUOTES by an invariant so
; that the new declarations cannot drift into a quote path while the old ones are held out of
; one.
pub const BRAIN_NODE : str = "brain:business_rules";
pub const BRAIN_READ_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
