; --- WHAT ELSE THE BRAIN PUBLISHES ABOUT THE TERM AXIS ------------------------------------
; The term axis is this file's own subject, so three further facts from the same node are
; recorded here rather than left for a reader to rediscover. None of them moves a band bound,
; and that is the point: each one is either a rule ABOUT the axis or a measurement AROUND it.
; --
; 1. WHERE THE SHOP STOPS NAMING A NUMBER AT ALL. brain:business_rules:450-457, the owner on
;    2026-08-21, explicitly not verified by data: from 180 days and longer the bot does not
;    name a price -- it says such a term is counted separately and hands the request to a
;    human, with no refusal, no invented number and no average. Shorter than 180 days nothing
;    changes. That line falls exactly on TERM_DAYS[5], the longest rung this file computes
;    with, and the 180-day totals pinned above stay legal for the same reason every other
;    number here does: they are audit arithmetic, and BANDS_PRODUCE_CLIENT_QUOTES is false.
;    The node also gives the reason the line was not drawn lower, in money: the 30-to-179 day
;    bucket carries 42 percent of all revenue at a miss of about 7.5 percent, and going silent
;    there would cost more than the miss (brain:business_rules:458-462).
; 2. THE FLAT TAIL HAS AN OWNER'S RULE BESIDE IT NOW, AND STILL NO PUBLISHED BAND.
;    brain:business_rules:435-445, the owner on 2026-08-17 and 2026-08-18: the long bucket is
;    NOT split into several steps -- "the step stays one" -- closing a fork a measurement had
;    opened about 30-60, 61-120 and longer than 120 days. This file reads the month band as "a
;    month or longer" and gets a flat tail from 30 days on; that reading is now CORROBORATED
;    by a rule, which is worth knowing and is not the same thing as a published band. The
;    tariff still publishes nothing past the month, so band_index_for_days keeps saying that
;    its extension is a reading, and the invariant below keeps saying it too.
; 3. THE OWNER HAS NAMED A BUCKET BOUNDARY, AND THE BRAIN REFUSES TO MAP IT.
;    brain:business_rules:1300-1322, the owner on 2026-09-06: "the term step: the bucket
;    boundary is 14", on the owner's word and no other basis. The node records in the same
;    breath that this changes no behaviour yet, that live code on the other side reads a grid
;    whose first bucket ends at 13, and that HOW the 14 lands on a grid -- 14 inside the base
;    bucket with the discount from 15, or another layout -- is a question for code and is
;    deliberately not derived there. This file's own reading already puts the fortnight at
;    DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT, the same integer; whether the owner's 14 means the same cut is
;    precisely what has not been published, so TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_IS_MAPPED is false and
;    band_index_for_days is not moved by a day on a guess.
; --
; A CORRECTION THIS NODE FORCES on a sentence above. DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT is introduced there as
; "NOT a rung of the measured ladder -- no observed term falls between 7 and 30 days". That is
; true of the SEED's observed_terms_days and false as a statement about observed rentals: the
; booking census of 2026-08-18 over 1243 bookings (brain:business_rules:494-529) puts 420 of
; them in the 7-to-14 day bucket and 137 in the 15-to-29 day bucket -- 557 rentals inside the
; 23-day hole the seed's ladder leaves between its first two rungs, more than a third of the
; corpus in the first and more than a tenth in the second. The seed's array is a PUBLISHED
; LADDER, not a census, and the fortnight band is named for a term people actually rent. Note
; the census cuts at 14/15 where this file cuts at 13/14, which is the same one-day question as
; point 3 and another reason not to settle it by preference.
pub const LONG_TERM_HUMAN_QUOTE_DAYS : i32 = 180;
pub const LONG_TERM_LINE_STATED_AT : str = "2026-08-21";
pub const LONG_TERM_LINE_CITATION : str = "brain:business_rules:450-457";
pub const LONG_TERM_STAYS_ONE_STEP : bool = true;
pub const LONG_TERM_ONE_STEP_CITATION : str = "brain:business_rules:435-445";
pub const TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_OWNER_WORD : i32 = 14;
pub const TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_STATED_AT : str = "2026-09-06";
pub const TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_IS_MAPPED : bool = false;
pub const TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_CITATION : str = "brain:business_rules:1300-1322";
pub const CENSUS_CITATION : str = "brain:business_rules:494-529";
pub const CENSUS_MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-08-18";
pub const CENSUS_BOOKINGS : i32 = 1243;
pub const CENSUS_7_TO_14_BOOKINGS : i32 = 420;
pub const CENSUS_15_TO_29_BOOKINGS : i32 = 137;

; Which published band a term of `days` falls in, or BAND_NONE.
; This mapping is a READING of the band names, not a published rule: the seed names the
; bands week / two_weeks / month and publishes no assignment table. The two absences at the
; two ends are NOT treated alike, and the difference is a choice rather than a measurement.
; Below a week, no published band name could cover the term at all, so the answer is
; BAND_NONE (D9: absent stays absent). Beyond a month, the term has exactly one candidate
; name and the shop demonstrably rents 90, 120, 150 and 180 days, so the month band is read
; as "a month or longer" and extended over them. That extension is what makes the tail flat
; from 30 days on; it does not prove the tail flat, because the tariff publishes nothing
; there. The function exists so that the ladder and the bands can be checked against each
; other instead of drifting apart, and so that the reading is explicit where a reader can
; see it. The door assigns the real discount (D11).
pub fn band_index_for_days(days: i32) i8 {
    if (days < DAYS_PER_WEEK) {
        return BAND_NONE;
    }
    if (days < DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT) {
        return 0;
    }
    if (days < DAYS_PER_MONTH) {
        return 1;
    }
    return 2;
}

; The served band ENDS, added 2026-09-22, measured from migrations/079_rental_terms.sql's VALUES
; rows: week 7..13, two_weeks 14..29, month from 30 with max_days NULL::INT. 079 derives each end
; as the day before the next band begins and says so in its own comment; band_index_for_days
; encodes the same contiguity through its `<` tests. Until this date only the starts were
; declared here, so a half-applied re-cut -- week's end moved to 14 while two_weeks still starts
; at 14 -- left two served bands overlapping on one day with nothing in this file to disagree.
; The month band's end is an absence (NULL), not a number, so it is declared as the boolean
; MONTH_BAND_HAS_A_LAST_DAY = false and never as a day count.
pub const WEEK_BAND_LAST_DAY : i32 = 13;
pub const TWO_WEEKS_BAND_LAST_DAY : i32 = 29;
pub const MONTH_BAND_HAS_A_LAST_DAY : bool = false;

; The published discount for a class, in basis points, or CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE.
; Keyed on the seed's class string, because that is the key class_discounts is published
; under; the u8 discriminants are bike-catalog.t27's and are deliberately not mirrored here.
; Total over the two published classes and closed everywhere else: an unrecognised class -- a
; misspelling, a different case, a body name, a family key, an empty string -- never yields a
; discount, because inventing one would be the same offence as inventing a price (D9, D11).
; Note which way the failure falls. Returning CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE is safe only if the caller
; branches on it; passing it through to the arithmetic quotes the PRE-discount tariff, which
; is the very overstatement the class discount exists to prevent.
pub fn class_discount_bp(class_name: str) i32 {
    if (class_name == "scooter") {
        return SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP;
    }
    if (class_name == "motorcycle") {
        return MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP;
    }
    return CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE;
}

; --- tests --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

; The rounding rule is checked against figures this file did not compute: the per-day
; column of reconciliation.checks, produced by the owner's quote sheet. The 2500 bp input is
; the 0.25 scooter class discount, appearing here as the measured INPUT of the one rule this
; file owns -- the rounding -- and not as a rate this file publishes; a fixture is not a
; second copy of a rate -- though the rate itself now has a home here too, as
; SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP in THE CLASS TABLE above. The literals stay in this test on
; purpose: the lookup is exercised against the same measured column by a separate test, so the
; two routes check each other instead of being merged into one.
; --
; WHAT STOOD HERE WAS FALSE, corrected 2026-09-20. The paragraph this replaces said the 0.25
; was already declared as a constant by two other specs in this tree -- specs/rental_terms.t27
; (SCOOTER_DISCOUNT, CLASS_DISCOUNT_VALUES) and specs/pricing_honesty.t27
; (SCOOTER_DISCOUNT_AT_RECONCILIATION) -- and concluded that this file must not become a third
; declaration site. Every clause of that has stopped being true. Both root-level files were
; deleted in the merge. (The inventory in this sentence was measured when the corpus was
; smaller and said eleven files under specs/turbobaby/; re-measured 2026-09-21, find specs -type f
; returns 43 -- specs/agents/turbobaby.t27 and the 42 under specs/turbobaby/, and nothing else.
; The correction matters here more than most places, because this paragraph's whole subject is a
; note that outlived its evidence, and a stale count inside it would be the same defect a second
; time.) Neither constant name survives anywhere, and
; a grep for them over specs/ still matches only the two paragraphs of this file that record the
; correction -- this one and the one in THE CLASS TABLE, three lines in total, re-measured
; 2026-09-21. So the rate was not declared twice,
; it was declared NOWHERE, and the note explaining its absence outlived the files it pointed
; at and went on authorising that absence in their name. A reason that cites
; deleted evidence is worse than no reason, because it reads as though it had been checked.
; What is true now: this file is the SINGLE declaration site, chosen because it already owns
; the integer basis-point form of this arithmetic and because the six rows below are the
; measurement that corroborates the scooter rate. D15 still gives the runtime arithmetic one
; home in src/trios/pricing.rs; that is an implementation, not a declaration of the rate.
; --
; Note also what 2500 is NOT here. TWO_WEEKS_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP above is also 2500, so
; audit_daily_thb(449, 2500) == 337 below is reachable down the class axis and down the term
; axis alike. The two figures coincide as arithmetic, not as meaning; see THE COMPOSITION.
; The same coincidence runs on the other rate too: MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP is 1500, which
; is WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP and TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP as well. Two axes, one integer, three
; meanings -- which is why the composition is left open below rather than guessed at.
test the_rounding_rule_reproduces_the_six_measured_grid_figures {
    assert audit_daily_thb(939, 2500) == 704;
    assert audit_daily_thb(998, 2500) == 749;
    assert audit_daily_thb(690, 2500) == 518;
    assert audit_daily_thb(790, 2500) == 593;
    assert audit_daily_thb(449, 2500) == 337;
    assert audit_daily_thb(2788, 2500) == 2091;
}

; Term length one: 7 days, TERM_DAYS[0], the week band at each bound.
; 449 x 0.94 = 422.06 -> 422/day, x 7 = 2954. 449 x 0.85 = 381.65 -> 382/day, x 7 = 2674.
test the_week_total_is_pinned_at_both_band_bounds {
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, WEEK_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP) == 422;
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, WEEK_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP, TERM_DAYS[0]) == 2954;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP) == 382;
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, TERM_DAYS[0]) == 2674;
}

; Term length two: 30 days, TERM_DAYS[1], the month band at each bound.
; 449 x 0.65 = 291.85 -> 292/day, x 30 = 8760. 449 x 0.50 = 224.5 -> 225/day, x 30 = 6750.
; The second line is where half-up earns its keep: half-down would give 224 and 6720.
test the_month_total_is_pinned_at_both_band_bounds {
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP) == 292;
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP, TERM_DAYS[1]) == 8760;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP) == 225;
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, TERM_DAYS[1]) == 6750;
}

; Term length three: 180 days, TERM_DAYS[5], the longest observed term. Under this file's
; reading it shares the month band with the 30-day rung, so the per-day rate is the SAME 292
; and 225 and only the day count changes: 292 x 180 = 52560, 225 x 180 = 40500. This is the
; flat tail as arithmetic -- arithmetic over a reading, not over a published band.
test the_six_month_total_is_pinned_and_reuses_the_month_rate {
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP, TERM_DAYS[5]) == 52560;
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, TERM_DAYS[5]) == 40500;
}

; The fortnight, 14 days, is the band's name rather than an observed rung.
; 449 x 0.85 = 381.65 -> 382/day, x 14 = 5348. 449 x 0.75 = 336.75 -> 337/day, x 14 = 4718.
test the_fortnight_total_is_pinned_at_both_band_bounds {
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP, DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT) == 5348;
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, TWO_WEEKS_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT) == 4718;
}

; The edge that refutes the issue's wording. The bands touch at 0.15, so a week at its best
; published discount and a fortnight at its worst are the same 382 THB/day. Non-increasing
; holds; strictly decreasing does not. The totals differ only because the days differ.
test the_touching_edge_gives_two_terms_one_daily_rate {
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP) == audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP);
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, DAYS_PER_WEEK) == 2674;
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP, DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT) == 5348;
}

; The two published factors, composed the two available ways, on the reference tariff at the
; month ceiling. 2500 bp is the class rate and 5000 bp the term bound; 6250 bp is the single
; net factor for the same pair (0.75 x 0.50 = 0.375). The answers differ by a baht a day.
; THE NAME OF THIS TEST CHANGED on 2026-09-21 and the asserts did not. It was
; composing_the_class_and_term_discounts_is_order_dependent, on the reading that the seed left
; an ORDER unpublished. The brain publishes the composition as a PRODUCT
; (brain:business_rules:228-229), and factors of a product commute, so an order was never what
; these two numbers measure. What they measure is where the ROUNDING falls, which is still
; unpublished and still worth 30 THB a month -- more than the day-versus-total rounding order
; this file did pin. Same divergence, correct reason.
test composing_the_two_published_factors_is_rounding_dependent {
    assert audit_daily_thb(audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, 2500), MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP) == 169;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, 6250) == 168;
}

; Each band is a well-formed interval, and the floors themselves climb. Ordered bounds are
; what makes "the representative of each band" well defined at all.
test every_band_is_a_well_formed_and_ordered_interval {
    assert WEEK_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP <= WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP <= TWO_WEEKS_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP <= MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert WEEK_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP <= TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP <= MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP;
}

test the_measured_ladder_is_strictly_increasing {
    assert TERM_DAYS[0] < TERM_DAYS[1];
    assert TERM_DAYS[1] < TERM_DAYS[2];
    assert TERM_DAYS[2] < TERM_DAYS[3];
    assert TERM_DAYS[3] < TERM_DAYS[4];
    assert TERM_DAYS[4] < TERM_DAYS[5];
}

; The issue's ladder in months and the seed's ladder in days are the same ladder. Checked
; rather than assumed, because the agreement is what licensed using the days. The week rung
; is not restated here: the last invariant in this file carries it as a module-wide claim,
; and one claim is typed once.
test the_issue_ladder_in_months_equals_the_measured_days {
    assert TERM_DAYS[1] == DAYS_PER_MONTH;
    assert TERM_DAYS[2] == DAYS_PER_MONTH * 3;
    assert TERM_DAYS[3] == DAYS_PER_MONTH * 4;
    assert TERM_DAYS[4] == DAYS_PER_MONTH * 5;
    assert TERM_DAYS[5] == DAYS_PER_MONTH * 6;
}

; Six rungs, three bands, and one band with no rung in it. The 90 and 180 day answers are
; this file's reading of "month", not a published assignment (see band_index_for_days).
test the_bands_and_the_ladder_line_up {
    assert band_index_for_days(TERM_DAYS[0]) == 0;
    assert band_index_for_days(DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT) == 1;
    assert band_index_for_days(TERM_DAYS[1]) == 2;
    assert band_index_for_days(TERM_DAYS[2]) == 2;
    assert band_index_for_days(TERM_DAYS[5]) == 2;
}

; Each served band ends the day before the next begins, and the reading agrees at both seams.
test the_served_bands_end_the_day_before_the_next_begins {
    assert WEEK_BAND_LAST_DAY == 13;
    assert TWO_WEEKS_BAND_LAST_DAY == 29;
    assert MONTH_BAND_HAS_A_LAST_DAY == false;
    assert band_index_for_days(WEEK_BAND_LAST_DAY) == 0;
    assert band_index_for_days(WEEK_BAND_LAST_DAY + 1) == 1;
    assert band_index_for_days(TWO_WEEKS_BAND_LAST_DAY) == 1;
    assert band_index_for_days(TWO_WEEKS_BAND_LAST_DAY + 1) == 2;
}

; The measurement that keeps this file honest about what it is, on BOTH bases, because the
; seed publishes neither. Applying the month band at its most generous published bound to
; the PRE-class-discount reference tariff gives 6750 for 30 days against a published 5000 --
; 1750 THB apart. Applying the same bound to the class-discounted 337/day, which is the
; seed's own reconciled grid figure for this model, gives 5070 -- 70 THB apart. The gap the
; band leaves is therefore either 1750 or 70 depending on an assumption nobody published,
; and "the closest the band can get" is not a sentence this file may write. A band is not a
; price, and no caller may present one as a quote.
test the_month_band_cannot_reproduce_the_published_monthly_price {
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, DAYS_PER_MONTH) == 6750;
    assert audit_total_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, DAYS_PER_MONTH) - REF_MONTHLY_LOW_SEASON_THB == 1750;
    assert audit_total_thb(audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, 2500), MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, DAYS_PER_MONTH) == 5070;
    assert audit_total_thb(audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, 2500), MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP, DAYS_PER_MONTH) - REF_MONTHLY_LOW_SEASON_THB == 70;
}

; The two families whose verdict REVERSES between the two bases, in integers. 7900 and 8900
; are the published monthly low-season figures of FORZA 300 and XMAX 300; 690 and 790 are
; their published pre-discount tariffs; audit_daily_thb(base, 2500) is their class-discounted
; per-day rate, 518 and 593, already pinned above from the reconciliation grid. Measured
; inputs, not a second copy of the price list: nothing here is a client-facing number, only
; an implied discount compared against a published bound.
; Against the pre-discount tariff both imply far more than the 5000 bp ceiling. Against the
; class-discounted rate both land INSIDE the published month band. Same seed, same two
; families, two bases, opposite answers -- and the seed does not say which basis is right.
test the_two_bases_disagree_about_whether_the_month_band_contains_the_monthly_price {
    assert BP_ONE - (7900 * BP_ONE) / (DAYS_PER_MONTH * 690) == 6184;
    assert BP_ONE - (8900 * BP_ONE) / (DAYS_PER_MONTH * 790) == 6245;
    assert BP_ONE - (7900 * BP_ONE) / (DAYS_PER_MONTH * audit_daily_thb(690, 2500)) == 4917;
    assert BP_ONE - (8900 * BP_ONE) / (DAYS_PER_MONTH * audit_daily_thb(790, 2500)) == 4998;
    assert 6184 > MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert 6245 > MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert 4917 < MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert 4917 > MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert 4998 < MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert 4998 > MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP;
}

; --- THE CLASS TABLE, checked -------------------------------------------------------------

; The two published rates, and the lookup that serves them. 2500 and 1500 are
; data/fleet_seed.json lines 107 and 108 at 10000 basis points to the unit. The ordering
; assert is not decoration: the seed discounts scooters HARDER than motorcycles, which is the
; opposite of the intuition that the more expensive class gets the bigger cut, and a silent
; swap of the two literals would otherwise typecheck and read plausibly.
test the_published_class_discounts_are_pinned_from_the_seed {
    assert SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP == 2500;
    assert MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP == 1500;
    assert class_discount_bp("scooter") == SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert class_discount_bp("motorcycle") == MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP > MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP;
}

; The basis points ARE the published fractions, proved in integers rather than asserted in a
; comment: 0.25 is 1/4 exactly, so 2500 x 4 must be one whole unit; 0.15 is 3/20 exactly, so
; 1500 x 20 must be three. Both hold with no remainder, which is what licenses calling the
; conversion exact instead of rounded. Written as a multiplication on purpose -- dividing
; 10000 by 4 would also pass if BP_ONE were wrong, because the error would cancel.
test the_class_basis_points_equal_the_seed_fractions_exactly {
    assert SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP * 4 == BP_ONE;
    assert MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP * 20 == BP_ONE * 3;
}

; Closed on everything else. Five ways to miss, all of them things a caller plausibly holds:
; an empty string, the wrong case, a plural, a synonym the seed does not use, and a family key
; from the catalogue. None yields a discount. This is the fail-closed half of the contract.
test an_unrecognised_class_never_yields_a_discount {
    assert class_discount_bp("") == CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE;
    assert class_discount_bp("Scooter") == CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE;
    assert class_discount_bp("scooters") == CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE;
    assert class_discount_bp("motorbike") == CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE;
    assert class_discount_bp("nmax-155") == CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE;
}

; The trap the sentinel sets, pinned so it cannot be walked into quietly. CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE
; is 0, and 0 basis points is arithmetically "charge the full tariff": handed to
; audit_daily_thb it gives back REF_BASE_THB_DAY unchanged, the PRE-discount 449 that
; field_notes.base_rate_thb_day says overstates a scooter by 33%. So an unknown class that is
; passed through instead of branched on does not merely fail to discount -- it quotes the one
; number D11 forbids. The last assert is the contrast: a KNOWN class always moves the number.
; The literal 0 is pinned HERE and nowhere else. Every other line about the sentinel compares
; against CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE on both sides, so all of them keep passing if the sentinel is
; moved -- including the audit_daily_thb line, because 1 bp off 449 still rounds back to 449.
; Without this one assert the whole sentinel story would be unfalsifiable.
test the_unset_class_sentinel_is_not_a_zero_discount {
    assert CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE == 0;
    assert class_discount_bp("moped") == CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE) == REF_BASE_THB_DAY;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, class_discount_bp("scooter")) < REF_BASE_THB_DAY;
}

; The lookup reproduces the externally measured column. Three of the six reconciliation rows
; are re-run with the discount coming from class_discount_bp instead of a literal, so the new
; declaration is tied to a number the owner's quote sheet produced and this file did not: 939
; -> 704, 449 -> 337, 2788 -> 2091. All six of those rows are scooters, which is the whole of
; the grid's evidence about the class axis, and MOTORCYCLE_RATE_IS_GRID_RECONCILED records
; that the other rate gets none of it.
test the_class_lookup_reproduces_the_seed_reconciled_grid {
    assert audit_daily_thb(939, class_discount_bp("scooter")) == 704;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, class_discount_bp("scooter")) == 337;
    assert audit_daily_thb(2788, class_discount_bp("scooter")) == 2091;
    assert MOTORCYCLE_RATE_IS_GRID_RECONCILED == false;
}

; The one piece of evidence the motorcycle rate does have, recomputed. field_notes in the same
; seed says quoting the raw tariff "overstates every scooter by 33% and every motorcycle by
; 18%". An overstatement is the base over the discounted rate, less one: BP_ONE x BP_ONE
; divided by the net, minus BP_ONE. That gives 3333 bp and 1764 bp -- 33.33% and 17.64%,
; which are the seed's 33% and its 18% rounded. This is a genuine second source: the sentence
; is written independently of the class_discounts block, and it agrees with both constants.
; Integer division truncates here, which is why the asserts name 3333 and 1764 rather than the
; seed's rounded pair; the rounding is the field note's, not this file's.
test the_seed_field_note_overstatement_corroborates_both_class_rates {
    assert (BP_ONE * BP_ONE) / (BP_ONE - SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP) - BP_ONE == 3333;
    assert (BP_ONE * BP_ONE) / (BP_ONE - MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP) - BP_ONE == 1764;
}

; The ROUNDING stays open, now tied to the lookup so the two cannot drift apart. A class rate
; is not a total and not a daily rate for a term: 337 is the reference tariff with the scooter
; rate applied and nothing else, and the moment a term is added the answer depends on where the
; rounding falls -- 169 stepwise against 168 as one fused factor. Until 2026-09-21 the first
; assert read CLASS_TERM_COMPOSITION_IS_PINNED == false and stood for the whole composition;
; the composition is published now, so the tripwire moved to the part that is not, and the
; three asserts under it are unchanged because they always measured that part.
test a_class_rate_alone_is_not_a_total {
    assert COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_IS_PINNED == false;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, class_discount_bp("scooter")) == 337;
    assert audit_daily_thb(audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, class_discount_bp("scooter")), MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP) == 169;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, 6250) == 168;
}

; Both ownership edges, asserted rather than merely declared. Without imports a REUSES_* string
; is the only way this file names another contract's territory, and a string nothing checks is
; a comment with a type. The last two asserts are the point of the edge: the owner named is
; someone ELSE, so a copy-paste that pointed one of them back at this module would fail here.
test the_named_owners_are_the_ones_this_file_defers_to {
    assert REUSES_PRICING_ID == "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
    assert REUSES_CATALOG_ID == "turbobaby/bike-catalog";
    assert REUSES_PRICING_ID != ID;
    assert REUSES_CATALOG_ID != ID;
}

; Two restatements resolved on 2026-09-24. The silence sentence is gone, not copied: the file names
; pricing-honesty's two declarations and declares none. The reference rate stays as a declared copy
; of a named owner declaration, and the arithmetic that reads it is unchanged.
test the_silence_sentence_and_the_reference_rate_name_their_owner {
    assert SILENCE_SENTENCE_IS_DECLARED_HERE == false;
    assert PRICING_SILENCE_DECLARATIONS.len == 2;
    assert PRICING_SILENCE_DECLARATIONS[0] == "SAY_HUMAN_QUOTES";
    assert PRICING_SILENCE_DECLARATIONS[1] == "MUST_SAY";
    assert BANDS_PRODUCE_CLIENT_QUOTES == false;
    assert RESTATEMENT_DROPPED_ON_RESOLUTION.len == 1;
    assert RESTATEMENT_DROPPED_ON_RESOLUTION[0] == "ON_SILENCE";
    assert RESTATEMENTS_RESOLVED_AT == "2026-09-24";
    assert REF_BASE_IS_A_COPY == true;
    assert REF_BASE_OWNER_DECLARATION == "CHEAPEST_IN_STOCK_DAY_RATE_THB";
    assert REF_BASE_SEED_FAMILY == "nmax-155";
    assert REF_MODEL == "NMAX 155";
    assert REUSES_PRICING_ID == "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE) == REF_BASE_THB_DAY;
}

; The 2026-09-12 ruling is cited at two ranges since the re-read of 2026-09-24: the owner's words
; and the source consequence at one, the silence consequence at the other.
test the_price_ruling_is_cited_where_each_clause_stands {
    assert PRICE_AUTHORITY_CITATION == "brain:business_rules:1661-1678";
    assert PRICE_ON_SILENCE_CITATION == "brain:business_rules:1684-1687";
    assert PRICE_ON_SILENCE_CITATION != PRICE_AUTHORITY_CITATION;
    assert PRICE_RULING_REREAD_AT == "2026-09-24";
    assert PRICE_RULING_REREAD_AT != BRAIN_READ_AT;
    assert COMPOSITION_PRODUCES_CLIENT_QUOTES == false;
}

; --- THE COMPOSITION, checked -------------------------------------------------------------

; The published composition as a shape: three factors, three provenances, and a citation a
; reader can take back to the node it came from. The provenance entries are compared against
; each other rather than only counted, because their whole point is that the three are NOT the
; same kind of fact, and an array that quietly became three copies of one string would still
; have length three.
test the_published_composition_is_a_product_of_three_named_factors {
    assert CLASS_TERM_COMPOSITION_IS_PINNED == true;
    assert COMPOSITION_FACTORS == 3;
    assert COMPOSITION_FACTOR_NAMES.len == 3;
    assert COMPOSITION_FACTOR_PROVENANCE.len == 3;
    assert COMPOSITION_FACTOR_NAMES[0] == "model base";
    assert COMPOSITION_FACTOR_NAMES[1] == "season factor";
    assert COMPOSITION_FACTOR_NAMES[2] == "term step";
    assert COMPOSITION_FACTOR_PROVENANCE[0] != COMPOSITION_FACTOR_PROVENANCE[1];
    assert COMPOSITION_FACTOR_PROVENANCE[1] != COMPOSITION_FACTOR_PROVENANCE[2];
    assert COMPOSITION_CITATION == "brain:business_rules:228-229";
}

; The half of the old refusal that survives, with the money that makes it worth keeping. The
; two roundings differ by one baht a day on the reference tariff and thirty on a month, and
; both figures are carried as constants so that an edit which "simplifies" the arithmetic has
; to change a number rather than a habit.
test the_rounding_between_the_factors_is_still_unpublished {
    assert COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_IS_PINNED == false;
    assert audit_daily_thb(audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP), MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP) - audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, 6250) == COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_GAP_THB_DAY;
    assert COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_GAP_THB_DAY * DAYS_PER_MONTH == COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_GAP_THB_MONTH;
}

; The sign, in integers, on the brain's own example magnitude. 494 is the tariff carrying a
; surcharge and 404 is the same magnitude misread as a discount: the shop's number is the
; first, and a caller who "corrects" the minus serves the second. The sixth assert is the cost
; of that misread ON THIS TARIFF -- 1821 bp against the correct price.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-21 BY REVIEW: this comment used to call 1821 "the brain's about twenty
; percent as an exact ratio" and "base-independent (0.9/1.1)", and it is neither. The eighth
; and ninth asserts are the correction, run rather than asserted in prose: the same ratio on a
; base of 1000 comes out 1818, which is what the convention alone gives, so 1821 is the baht
; rounding at 449 and not a property of the convention. And the node says "about twenty
; percent" with no denominator named -- against the base the gap is exactly twenty percent,
; against the correct price 18.18 -- so no exact figure here is the owner's. The last assert is
; the node's own caveat, carried rather than dropped: this rule is the owner's stated intention
; and was not yet confirmed by data when it was written.
test a_minus_moves_the_price_up_and_reading_it_as_a_discount_moves_it_down {
    assert PEAK_EXAMPLE_SURCHARGE_BP + PEAK_EXAMPLE_MISREAD_AS_DISCOUNT_BP == 0;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_SURCHARGE_BP) == 494;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_MISREAD_AS_DISCOUNT_BP) == 404;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_SURCHARGE_BP) > REF_BASE_THB_DAY;
    assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_MISREAD_AS_DISCOUNT_BP) < REF_BASE_THB_DAY;
    assert (audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_SURCHARGE_BP) - audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_MISREAD_AS_DISCOUNT_BP)) * BP_ONE / audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_SURCHARGE_BP) == SIGN_MISREAD_UNDERSTATEMENT_BP;
    assert SIGN_MISREAD_UNDERSTATEMENT_IS_BASE_INDEPENDENT == false;
    assert (audit_daily_thb(SIGN_MISREAD_PROBE_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_SURCHARGE_BP) - audit_daily_thb(SIGN_MISREAD_PROBE_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_MISREAD_AS_DISCOUNT_BP)) * BP_ONE / audit_daily_thb(SIGN_MISREAD_PROBE_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_SURCHARGE_BP) == SIGN_MISREAD_UNDERSTATEMENT_WITHOUT_ROUNDING_BP;
    assert SIGN_MISREAD_UNDERSTATEMENT_WITHOUT_ROUNDING_BP != SIGN_MISREAD_UNDERSTATEMENT_BP;
    assert SIGN_CONVENTION_IS_DATA_CONFIRMED == false;
}

; The two class rates read as what the brain says they are: the magnitude of the season factor
; at the bottom of the deep low season, against the ceiling of the March-to-May transition
; further up the same calendar. Both published magnitudes are deeper than that ceiling, which
; is the arithmetic of "different places in the calendar, not a contradiction". The last
; assert is a coincidence pinned so it cannot be mistaken for a derivation: 1000 bp is also the
; width of the gap between the fortnight and month bands, and the two have nothing to do with
; each other.
test the_class_rates_are_the_deep_low_season_magnitude {
    assert CLASS_DISCOUNTS_ARE_A_CLASS_AXIS == false;
    assert CLASS_DISCOUNTS_ARE_SEASONAL_MAGNITUDE == true;
    assert DEEP_LOW_SEASON_MONTHS == "June-October";
    assert TRANSITION_MONTHS == "March-May";
    assert SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP > TRANSITION_CEILING_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP > TRANSITION_CEILING_DISCOUNT_BP;
    assert TRANSITION_CEILING_DISCOUNT_BP == MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP - TWO_WEEKS_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP;
}

; The money check and the floor under it, as published. The subtraction is asserted at 1080
; and the published difference at 1090 on purpose: the node states all three figures, they are
; rounded independently, and an edit that "fixed" one of them to make the arithmetic close
; would have to delete an assert to do it. That is the only way this file lets a published
; number be overruled -- visibly.
test the_formula_was_checked_with_money_and_carries_its_floor {
    assert PEAK_SHELF_BOOKINGS == 260;
    assert PEAK_SHELF_MEDIAN_MISS_BP == -60;
    assert NO_SEASON_CONTROL_MISS_BP == 2140;
    assert OWNER_CALENDAR_MISS_BP == 1060;
    assert ACCURACY_FLOOR_BP == OWNER_CALENDAR_MISS_BP;
    assert NO_SEASON_CONTROL_MISS_BP - OWNER_CALENDAR_MISS_BP == 1080;
    assert CALENDAR_EARNS_BP == 1090;
    assert CALENDAR_EARNS_BP - (NO_SEASON_CONTROL_MISS_BP - OWNER_CALENDAR_MISS_BP) == 10;
    assert ACCURACY_FLOOR_IS_REDUCIBLE == false;
    assert UNOBSERVABLES.len == 3;
}

; The floor in baht, beside the two divergences this file spends paragraphs on. 47 THB a day
; is 10.6 percent of the reference tariff; the rounding gaps are 1 and 4. Both kinds of number
; are worth having and they are not the same kind: the small ones are two implementations of
; one rule disagreeing, which is a defect, and the large one is the honest width of the rule.
; Asserted rather than left in prose, because prose is what goes stale.
test the_accuracy_floor_dwarfs_the_rounding_questions {
    assert REF_BASE_THB_DAY * ACCURACY_FLOOR_BP / BP_ONE == 47;
    assert REF_BASE_THB_DAY * ACCURACY_FLOOR_BP / BP_ONE > COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_GAP_THB_DAY * 40;
    assert COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_GAP_THB_DAY < 4;
}

; The refusal that stays, asserted so it cannot be dropped in silence. No month's coefficient
; is declared in this repository; the sheet they live in is named, foreign and live, and the
; calendar that indexes them is the owner's rule rather than a measurement.
test the_month_by_month_season_table_is_still_refused {
    assert MONTHLY_SEASON_COEFFICIENTS_ARE_DECLARED == false;
    assert SEASON_COEFFICIENT_CITATION == "brain:business_rules:95-96";
    assert SEASON_CALENDAR_IS_OWNER_RULE == true;
    assert SEASON_CALENDAR_IS_DATA_VERIFIED == false;
    assert SEASON_CALENDAR_OVERRIDES_BOOKING_HISTORY == true;
}

; The three further term-axis facts, checked against this ladder, and the census that corrects
; a sentence in the header. 557 rentals fall inside the 23-day hole the seed's ladder leaves
; between its first two rungs -- more than a third of the corpus in the first bucket and more
; than a tenth in the second -- so the fortnight band is named for something people rent, even
; though no rung of the published ladder names it.
test the_brain_term_axis_facts_hold_against_this_ladder {
    assert TERM_DAYS[5] == LONG_TERM_HUMAN_QUOTE_DAYS;
    assert LONG_TERM_STAYS_ONE_STEP == true;
    assert TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_OWNER_WORD == DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT;
    assert TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_IS_MAPPED == false;
    assert TERM_DAYS[1] - TERM_DAYS[0] == 23;
    assert CENSUS_7_TO_14_BOOKINGS + CENSUS_15_TO_29_BOOKINGS == 557;
    assert CENSUS_7_TO_14_BOOKINGS * 3 > CENSUS_BOOKINGS;
    assert CENSUS_15_TO_29_BOOKINGS * 10 > CENSUS_BOOKINGS;
}

; --- invariants ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Claims about the whole module that no single example carries.

; The ladder and the band list are the measured ones. A rung or a band silently dropped
; fails here instead of passing as a tidy-up: a count of zero is always a bug (D16), and a
; count of five would mean this spec had quietly stopped describing the tariff.
invariant the_measured_ladder_holds_six_rungs
  assert TERM_DAYS.len == 6

invariant the_published_bands_are_three
  assert BAND_NAMES.len == 3

; The served bands are contiguous: no day falls in two bands and none between two. Stated on the
; declared ends and starts, which the source gate reads from the same 079 rows.
invariant every_served_band_ends_the_day_before_the_next_begins
  assert WEEK_BAND_LAST_DAY + 1 == DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT and TWO_WEEKS_BAND_LAST_DAY + 1 == DAYS_PER_MONTH and WEEK_BAND_LAST_DAY >= DAYS_PER_WEEK and MONTH_BAND_HAS_A_LAST_DAY == false

; THE MONOTONICITY CLAIM, in the only form the tariff supports: the daily rate is
; NON-INCREASING as the term lengthens, stated on a well-defined representative of each
; band -- floor against floor, then ceiling against ceiling.
; Stated THROUGH audit_daily_thb, at the rounded baht, on purpose. The same claim written as
; REF_BASE_THB_DAY * (BP_ONE - X) >= REF_BASE_THB_DAY * (BP_ONE - Y) would scale both sides
; by one positive constant and reduce to X <= Y, which is a comparison of two named bounds
; and is already pinned by every_band_is_a_well_formed_and_ordered_interval above; it would
; also say nothing about the function that the runtimes actually call. In the form below the
; rounding is inside the claim, so an edit to audit_daily_thb that broke the order -- a
; half-down divide, a sign slip in the net basis points -- fails here.
; What is claimed and what is not: the unrounded order follows from the bound order for every
; non-negative tariff, while the four asserts below are pinned on the one reference tariff,
; because that is the tariff this file computes with.
invariant the_rounded_daily_rate_never_rises_from_the_week_floor_to_the_fortnight_floor
  assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, WEEK_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP) >= audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP)

invariant the_rounded_daily_rate_never_rises_from_the_fortnight_floor_to_the_month_floor
  assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP) >= audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP)

invariant the_rounded_daily_rate_never_rises_from_the_week_ceiling_to_the_fortnight_ceiling
  assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP) >= audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, TWO_WEEKS_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP)

invariant the_rounded_daily_rate_never_rises_from_the_fortnight_ceiling_to_the_month_ceiling
  assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, TWO_WEEKS_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP) >= audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, MONTH_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP)

; The flat tail, as a claim about the reading rather than about the tariff: under
; band_index_for_days every rung from the month on answers with one band, so all four
; unpublished rungs answer exactly as the 30-day rung does. If the reading is ever narrowed
; -- the honest alternative is BAND_NONE beyond a month, since the tariff publishes nothing
; there -- this invariant is the thing that has to change, which is where the decision
; belongs.
invariant every_rung_from_the_month_on_shares_one_band
  assert band_index_for_days(TERM_DAYS[1]) == band_index_for_days(TERM_DAYS[5])

; The other end of the same question, and the one the tariff does answer: one day short of
; the first published band there is no band, not a zero discount (D9). Stated against
; DAYS_PER_WEEK rather than against the literal 6, so that it follows the band if the band
; ever moves.
invariant a_term_one_day_short_of_the_first_band_has_no_band
  assert band_index_for_days(DAYS_PER_WEEK - 1) == BAND_NONE

; Why the inequality above is >= and not >. The first two bands SHARE an endpoint at 1500
; bp (0.15), so one daily rate serves the longest week and the shortest fortnight. This is
; pinned as an invariant precisely because it is the fact that refutes the stricter claim:
; if a later edit separated the bands, the stricter claim would become available and this
; assert would be the thing that had to be deleted to get there.
invariant the_week_and_fortnight_bands_touch_at_fifteen_percent
  assert WEEK_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP == TWO_WEEKS_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP

; The other junction has a hole, not a shared endpoint: 0.35 - 0.25 = 0.10, 1000 bp that
; the tariff publishes nothing for. Recorded rather than closed by interpolation, the same
; way the unpublished delivery areas render as a dash instead of a number derived from
; Bangtao. The three bands are not a partition of anything.
invariant the_fortnight_and_month_bands_leave_a_gap
  assert MONTH_MIN_DISCOUNT_BP - TWO_WEEKS_MAX_DISCOUNT_BP == 1000

; D11, mechanically. Nothing in this file may be served to a client as a price: the
; functions pin arithmetic, and the door quotes. Flipping this constant to true is the one
; edit that would turn an audit instrument into an invented quote, so it fails here.
invariant no_band_ever_becomes_a_client_quote
  assert BANDS_PRODUCE_CLIENT_QUOTES == false

; The scope of the file, mechanically, and the one edit in this file's history where a
; tripwire was allowed to fire. This invariant used to read
; CLASS_TERM_COMPOSITION_IS_PINNED == false and was the guard on the composition refusal; on
; 2026-09-21 the refusal was answered by a published rule with a citation and tests behind it,
; which is the one condition the old comment named for flipping it. The guard did not
; disappear with the refusal -- it moved to the half that is still unpublished. Flipping
; COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_IS_PINNED to true without a published rounding rule and a test behind it
; fails here, exactly as before.
invariant the_composition_rounding_is_left_open
  assert COMPOSITION_ROUNDING_IS_PINNED == false

; The legacy snapshot keeps its old ID so discovery cannot silently content-dedupe it with the
; canonical owner while it is under review.
invariant the_root_snapshot_carries_a_legacy_id
  assert ID != TWIN_SPEC_ID

; Ownership is no longer ambiguous: this ID and the declaration matrix name the survivor.
invariant the_twin_semantic_merge_is_resolved
  assert TWIN_IS_RESOLVED == true and TWIN_MERGE_MATRIX == "docs/t27-semantic-merge-matrix.md"

; The corpus size, so the next growth spurt breaks an assert instead of quietly falsifying two
; paragraphs of this header the way the last one did.
; Corrected 2026-09-22: it does not. The assert compares three of this file's own constants, so a
; growth spurt in the tree breaks nothing; 14b01ac added two specs on 2026-09-21 and 42 + 1 == 43
; stayed green. What it does hold is the split adding up to the total within each dated reading.
invariant the_corpus_count_is_the_sum_of_its_two_directories
  assert CORPUS_FILES_UNDER_TURBOBABY + CORPUS_FILES_UNDER_AGENTS == CORPUS_FILES and CORPUS_FILES_UNDER_TURBOBABY_REMEASURED + CORPUS_FILES_UNDER_AGENTS_REMEASURED == CORPUS_FILES_REMEASURED

; The claim the stale counts were supporting, and the only one that has to stay true for
; TWIN_SPEC_PATH to be a former address: the root of specs/ holds no .t27.
invariant the_deleted_drafts_slot_is_still_empty
  assert CORPUS_ROOT_T27_FILES == 0 and CORPUS_ROOT_T27_FILES_REMEASURED == 0

; The shortest published band starts at a week, so the ladder's first rung is a week and
; anything shorter has no band. Absent stays absent (D9); it is not a zero discount.
invariant the_ladder_starts_where_the_first_band_starts
  assert TERM_DAYS[0] == DAYS_PER_WEEK

; THE CLASS TABLE IS TOTAL over exactly the classes the seed publishes. Both keys answer, and
; both answer with their own rate -- a lookup that fell through to the sentinel for a
; published class would be the silent version of losing the rate again, which is the defect
; this table was added to repair.
invariant the_class_discount_table_is_total_over_the_classes_the_seed_publishes
  assert class_discount_bp("scooter") == SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP and class_discount_bp("motorcycle") == MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP

; And closed everywhere else: nothing outside those two keys ever yields a discount. Stated
; against CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE rather than against 0, so that it follows the sentinel if the
; sentinel ever moves off zero.
invariant the_class_discount_table_yields_nothing_for_any_other_input
  assert class_discount_bp("moped") == CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE and class_discount_bp("") == CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE

; Neither published rate may be zero. This is the specific regression that the deleted root
; twins allowed: with no declaration anywhere, every caller's class discount was effectively
; absent, and absent reads as the full tariff. A rate that went to the sentinel value would
; reproduce that state while still looking like a table.
invariant a_published_class_rate_is_never_the_unset_sentinel
  assert SCOOTER_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP != CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE and MOTORCYCLE_CLASS_DISCOUNT_BP != CLASS_DISCOUNT_NONE


; --- invariants the published composition brings with it ----------------------------------

; The composition, mechanically. Three factors and the flip that made them declarable: an edit
; that drops a factor, or that reopens the composition without saying so, fails here.
invariant the_composition_is_the_published_three_factor_product
  assert CLASS_TERM_COMPOSITION_IS_PINNED == true and COMPOSITION_FACTORS == 3

; The refusal that stays, as an invariant rather than as a paragraph. The season numbers live
; in a sheet this side can only read, and no edit may declare one of them here.
invariant the_month_by_month_season_coefficients_are_never_declared_here
  assert MONTHLY_SEASON_COEFFICIENTS_ARE_DECLARED == false

; The sign, in the only form that survives an edit to audit_daily_thb: a minus is a surcharge,
; so it must land ABOVE the same magnitude read as a discount. Stated through the function at
; the rounded baht, for the same reason the monotonicity invariants above are.
invariant a_minus_never_reads_as_a_discount
  assert audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_SURCHARGE_BP) > audit_daily_thb(REF_BASE_THB_DAY, PEAK_EXAMPLE_MISREAD_AS_DISCOUNT_BP)

; The framing that made the old refusal wrong rather than merely incomplete: the two published
; class rates are the season factor at one place in the calendar, not an axis of their own.
invariant the_class_rates_are_not_an_axis_of_their_own
  assert CLASS_DISCOUNTS_ARE_A_CLASS_AXIS == false and CLASS_DISCOUNTS_ARE_SEASONAL_MAGNITUDE == true

; A rule is not a measurement. The calendar overrides the booking history and is not checked
; against it, and nothing in this file may present it as a measured fact.
invariant the_season_calendar_is_a_rule_and_never_a_measurement
  assert SEASON_CALENDAR_IS_OWNER_RULE == true and SEASON_CALENDAR_IS_DATA_VERIFIED == false

; The floor, with the reason it is a floor. Three unobservables hold it up, and it does not
; come down until they start being recorded; declaring it reducible means deleting this line.
invariant the_accuracy_floor_waits_on_three_unobservables
  assert ACCURACY_FLOOR_IS_REDUCIBLE == false and UNOBSERVABLES.len == 3

; D11 for the new declarations, tied to the old constant instead of restated: whatever the
; composition becomes, it stays on the same side of the door as the bands.
invariant the_published_composition_is_no_more_quotable_than_the_bands
  assert COMPOSITION_PRODUCES_CLIENT_QUOTES == BANDS_PRODUCE_CLIENT_QUOTES

; The owner's line, where the shop stops naming a number at all, falls exactly on the longest
; rung this file computes with. If either ever moves, this is where the two stop agreeing.
invariant the_longest_rung_is_where_the_shop_stops_naming_a_number
  assert TERM_DAYS[5] == LONG_TERM_HUMAN_QUOTE_DAYS

; The owner's bucket boundary is a word, not a mapping. Until the brain says how the 14 lands
; on a grid, band_index_for_days does not move by a day on anybody's preference -- and the
; integer this file already uses for that cut is the same 14, which is what makes the
; temptation worth an invariant.
invariant the_owner_bucket_boundary_stays_unmapped
  assert TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_IS_MAPPED == false and TERM_BUCKET_BOUNDARY_OWNER_WORD == DAYS_PER_FORTNIGHT
